> > > > > >
> > > > > > The parameters that are not fitting well are mostly the intercepts for both alpha and beta, as well as several of the beta estimates. And unfortunately, the community level parameters also don't seem to be sampling very well. Furthermore, the trace plots on the factor loadings show poor convergence for many species.
> > > > > >
> > > > > > So I have a few questions about what I might do to improve convergence, sampling efficiency, and GOF. You have at least three suggestions in your 'convergence issues vignette <https://doserlab.com/files/spoccupancy-web/articles/modelconsiderations#identifiability-of-the-spatial-factors-factor-loadings-and-species-specific-intercepts-in-spatial-factor-models>': 1) consider the order of the species, 2) using more factors, or 3) fit one chain. I’m curious whether you think any of these might be particularly helpful in my case, and how you would approach them in practice.
